## Run7 — Rider notifications & messages (investigation 03:57–04:10 UTC, read-only)

Rider device (`dumpsys notification --noredact`, history disabled so only the active notifications are visible) — **only ONE notification from sn.galass.galassrider** for the whole session (rides #251, #252, #253):
- posted 03:42:16 UTC (ride #253 start), channel `high_importance_channel` ("High Importance Notifications"), importance 4 (HIGH), shown heads-up (airtime 4.2 s), BigTextStyle, small icon `@mipmap/ic_launcher`
- title: `Galass`
- text: `hi hejjjdb jjejjdb (hhhjjhvevdb), Ride Id : WFOOKBKDNB \r\nService :  Voiture\r\nRider: hhhjjhvevdb\r\nRide Amount : 1 170XOF\r\nMHV3+674, Rue CO 38, Dakar, Senegal to Place de l'Indépendance, place de l'indépendance, Dakar, Senegal. Duration - 12 mins, Distance - 4.683 km.\r\nPickup Time -  19-10-2026 03:42`
Server: `notification_logs` #48 (user 13, firebase push, subject "Ride has started", 03:42:13) is the only rider push since 03:25. Screens: `run7-rider-notif-01-shade.png`, `run7-rider-notif-02-activity.png`.

How it works: backend `notify()` → `app/Notify/Push.php` sends FCM `notification{title,body}` with title = `template.push_title ?? gs('push_title')`. Rider `push_notification_service.dart`: foreground → `flutter_local_notifications` re-post (channel high_importance_channel, icon `@mipmap/ic_launcher`, `fullScreenIntent: true`, `BigTextStyleInformation('')`); background handler is empty, so the system tray shows the FCM notification. Ride state changes (DRIVER_ASSIGNED, PICK_UP, RIDE_END, CASH_PAYMENT_RECEIVED, CANCEL_RIDE from the dispatch sweep, MESSAGE_RECEIVED) are sent **only through Pusher** (`EventsRide`), not FCM.

| ID | Sev | Issue | Expected vs actual | Evidence | Suspected file / fix |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| N-1 | P1 | **Rider push only on "ride started"**. No push for: driver assigned/accepted (DRIVER_ASSIGNED is Pusher only; the ACCEPT_RIDE template is sent to the *driver* in the bid flow), ride ended (RIDE_END Pusher only), payment confirmed (RIDE_PAYMENT_COMPLETE goes to the driver), **no driver available / auto-cancel** (#251, #252: no notification_logs row, Pusher CANCEL_RIDE only). With the app in background or killed, the rider is not told the driver is coming or that the request failed. | Push (FR) at least for: chauffeur trouvé, chauffeur arrivé/course démarrée, course terminée + montant, aucun chauffeur, annulation | notification_logs since 03:25 = only #48; `DispatchOrchestrator.php:292,343`, `Api/Driver/RideController.php:81,190,319` | add `notify($ride->user, …)` calls + templates |
| N-2 | P1 | **Push text in English, not French**, and written for the driver: "hi … Ride Id … Service … **Rider: hhhjjhvevdb** (the recipient's own username) … Ride Amount : 1 170XOF … Duration - 12 mins … Pickup Time -". Starts with lowercase "hi" and shows full name + username. | Short French text, e.g. « Votre course a démarré — Papa Diallo, Toyota rouge AA456YY » | `run7-rider-notif-01-shade.png`, notification_templates START_RIDE (#31), global push template | Rewrite templates in FR (START_RIDE, CANCEL_RIDE, ACCEPT_RIDE…), drop "Rider:" for the rider |
| N-3 | P2 | **Generic title "Galass"**: START_RIDE `push_title` is NULL, so the title falls back to gs push_title. The subject "Ride has started" never appears on the device. Same for most ride templates (ACCEPT_RIDE, BID_REJECT, NEW_RIDE…). | Title = event (« Course démarrée ») | dumpsys `android.title=Galass` | fill `push_title` per template, or fall back to `subject` in `Push.php::getTitle()` |

